From 5403fa3aee6005ea69f4b83cfb513fa59403129e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:19:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] [TRANSLATION] Add Finnish (fi-FI) to the event log, I/O
 error and PCI class message tables

Problem: The event log and Service Control Manager's messages, the I/O
errors drivers log, and the PCI device class names Device Manager shows
had no Finnish.

Why: They are shown to the user in Event Viewer and Device Manager.

How: Add Finnish=0x40B and a Finnish block to every message of
neteventmsg.mc, ntiologc.mc and pciclass.mc, with the same %1, %n and %0
inserts as the English. The tables compile with windmc.
